# SCSS Nesting

- Keep new selector nesting shallow; target a maximum of three levels for newly added rules.
- Prefer modifier classes, data attributes, or small helper classes over deep descendant chains.
- One extra nesting level is acceptable for state selectors, aria attributes, or shared mixin wrappers when flattening would reduce clarity.
- When editing legacy SCSS, improve local nesting if practical, but do not refactor large files just to satisfy this rule.

### How to verify

Review a changed SCSS block and confirm newly added selectors stay at three nesting levels or less unless the extra level is a justified state or wrapper case, and that no broad legacy-only refactor was introduced.
